<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Jevio adaptive-icon foreground: the same mark, fitted to the launcher's safe zone.
     An adaptive icon is 108x108 but a launcher may mask it to a 66-wide circle, so the artwork has
     to fit that circle rather than the square. This mark is unusually hostile to that: the three
     satellites sit at opposite diagonal corners, so what matters is the distance from the artwork's
     centre to the farthest corner — the bottom-left square, 66 units out in source space. Scaling
     by 0.5 brings that to 33, exactly the safe radius, so nothing clips on a round mask.
     The translate centres the artwork's bounding box (50, 49.95) on (54, 54); centring the viewport
     instead would sit it low and left, because the box is not symmetric about the viewBox. -->
